# Aegis patch 191 - widget cleanup + Aegis ID session persistence
# r147 follow-up report (2026-11-28):
#   1. Widget picker pages still titled 'Chromium bookmarks' and
#      'Chromium search' - the upstream label resources are not
#      rebrandable, so the manifest receivers carry Aegis literals
#      (same approach as patch 190 for the quick action widget).
#   2. The Dino widget variant is gone for good: the Dino page was
#      removed from the browser, so initialize() now disables the Dino
#      component (launchers drop it from the picker) and the quick
#      action widget no longer offers the Dino button.
#   3. Aegis ID session persistence: tokens and the vault key lived only
#      in memory, so every restart demanded a fresh sign-in before
#      password sync resumed ('sign in to Aegis ID' on second launch).
#      The session is now sealed with a non-exportable AndroidKeyStore
#      AES-GCM key into one prefs blob and restored in the constructor;
#      token rotations (adopt) re-seal, sign-out clears.
# Staged alphabetically after 190.

